\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Illustration of the space-then-time attention masking pattern used in the backbone architecture. The left and middle figure show the two subsequent steps of the spatial attention mask, where the middle figure shows the shifted attention window, and the right figure shows the temporal attention mask. Indirectly, every token can attend to every other token in the input sequence, negligibly affecting predictive performance while being more efficient than a memory-intensive spatiotemporal attention approach.}}{25}{figure.caption.21}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:BlockExplainer}{{5.1}{25}{Illustration of the space-then-time attention masking pattern used in the backbone architecture. The left and middle figure show the two subsequent steps of the spatial attention mask, where the middle figure shows the shifted attention window, and the right figure shows the temporal attention mask. Indirectly, every token can attend to every other token in the input sequence, negligibly affecting predictive performance while being more efficient than a memory-intensive spatiotemporal attention approach}{figure.caption.21}{}}
